**This is intentional behaviour — but here's how to work around it.**

When a product is **newly created** in APIM, Azure automatically generates some resources (a default group and optionally a built-in subscription). The publisher removes these auto-created resources to ensure APIM stays consistent with your source-control artifacts. The relevant code and comment in `tools/code/publisher/Product.cs` explains the rationale:

```csharp
// Delete automatically created resources if the product is new. This ensures that APIM is consistent with source control.
if (productAlreadyExists is false)
{
    await deleteAutomaticallyCreatedProductGroups(name, cancellationToken);
    await deleteAutomaticallyCreatedProductSubscriptions(name, cancellationToken);
}
```

An automatically-created subscription is identified by having **no display name** and an owner of `/users/1`.

**Workaround**: If you want a subscription to exist on the product after publishing, add it to your artifacts folder (`subscriptions/<name>/subscriptionInformation.json`) referencing the product. The publisher will then create it as a managed subscription, and it will not be removed by the auto-cleanup logic.

If you believe the auto-cleanup should be optional (configurable), feel free to open a feature-request issue or upvote any existing enhancement proposals.
